{
  "_doc": [
    "Byte-exact FTMS golden vectors (BRIEF 4.3). Owned by trainer-core; tests/trainer/test_ftms_codec.gd runs every case against FtmsCodec, and tools/trainer_bridge's Python tests reuse this file.",
    "Bytes are lower-case hex strings without separators; little-endian; 16-bit UUIDs on the Bluetooth base UUID.",
    "encode: {name, op, args, hex}. Ops: request_control {}, reset {}, start_resume {}, stop_pause {param: 1 stop | 2 pause}, target_power {watts}, target_resistance {level, encoding: 'uint8_0.1' | 'sint16_0.1'}, indoor_bike_simulation {wind_mps, grade_pct, crr, cw}, indoor_bike_data {record fields as in parse}. Scaling: value x 10^n (wind 1000, grade 100, crr 10000, cw 100, resistance 10, speed 100, cadence 2, met 10), rounded half away from zero (0.125 % grade -> 13, -0.125 -> -13), then clamped to the field range (sint16 -32768..32767, uint8 0..255, uint16 0..65535, uint24 0..16777215). target_power clamps to 0..32767 (never a negative target). indoor_bike_data sets More Data (bit 0) when speed_kmh is absent; the three energy fields travel together.",
    "parse: {name, kind, hex, valid, expect}. Kinds: indoor_bike_data, feature, power_range, resistance_range, machine_status, control_response, cycling_power_measurement. valid false means the parser rejects the bytes (GDScript: push_error and returns {}); otherwise expect is the complete output: every key present and no others. Scaled values decode as raw / 10^n (so 3050 -> 30.5); unscaled values are integers; 'params' (machine_status, control_response) is the hex of the bytes after the op code (resp. after the result code).",
    "Indoor Bike Data keys, in flag-bit order: flags, more_data (bit 0 set), speed_kmh (present when bit 0 is CLEAR, u16 0.01 km/h), avg_speed_kmh (bit 1, u16 0.01), cadence_rpm (bit 2, u16 0.5 rpm), avg_cadence_rpm (bit 3), distance_m (bit 4, u24 m), resistance_level (bit 5, s16, unitless), power_w (bit 6, s16 W), avg_power_w (bit 7, s16), total_energy_kcal (bit 8, u16) + energy_per_hour_kcal (u16) + energy_per_minute_kcal (u8), heart_rate_bpm (bit 9, u8), met (bit 10, u8 0.1), elapsed_s (bit 11, u16), remaining_s (bit 12, u16). Every field is bounds-checked; trailing bytes and the reserved bits 13-15 are ignored.",
    "machine_status decodes: 0x02 stop_pause (u8), 0x07 target_resistance (u8 0.1), 0x08 target_power_w (s16), 0x12 wind_mps/grade_pct/crr/cw (as Set Indoor Bike Simulation), 0x14 spin_down_status (u8), 0x15 target_cadence_rpm (u16 0.5); a known code with too few parameter bytes is invalid; other codes keep only code and params. control_response: 0x80, request_opcode, result, params; fewer than 3 bytes or a first byte other than 0x80 is invalid. cycling_power_measurement: flags (u16), power_w (s16), then pedal_power_balance_pct (bit 0, u8 0.5), accumulated_torque_nm (bit 2, u16 1/32), wheel_revs (bit 4, u32) + wheel_event_time_s (u16 1/2048 s), crank_revs (bit 5, u16) + crank_event_time_s (u16 1/1024 s); later fields ignored.",
    "assemble: {name, kind: indoor_bike_data, hex: [notifications in order], expect: [completed records], errors}. One assembler runs over the list. A part with More Data set is merged (later parts win, flags OR-ed) until a part with More Data clear completes the record: then bit 0 of the merged flags is cleared, more_data is false and parts counts the notifications. A part that repeats a field already pending first flushes the pending record incomplete (more_data true, flags as OR-ed). A malformed part is dropped (one error each; the pending record is kept). A record still pending at the end is not returned."
  ],
